# Accessibility audit: Label (2026-11-15)

Scope: `spec/components/label/contract.json`, `src/components/label/*`, `playwright/tests/label/*`. Standard: WCAG 2.2 AA, native label naming rules, SB-0009 (ID references do not cross shadow roots).

## Criteria

| POUR | Criterion | Result | Evidence |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| P | 1.4.3 text contrast | Pass | Contract pair `label.fg` on `color.background`; `npm run check` T6 passes; computed colour `rgb(10, 10, 10)` |
| P | 1.4.11 non-text contrast | Not applicable | No borders or indicators; the label is plain text |
| P | 1.4.1 color alone | Pass | Disabled is dimmed (opacity 0.5) and the associated control is also natively disabled; no meaning by color |
| P | forced-colors | Pass | Probe with `forced-colors: active`: text computes to `rgb(0, 0, 0)` (CanvasText); no background or border to lose |
| P | prefers-reduced-motion | Not applicable | No transition or animation (`transition-duration: 0s`) |
| O | 2.1.1 / 2.4.7 / 2.1.2 keyboard, focus, trap | Pass | Host `tabIndex` -1, no role, no focusable parts (spec "is not focusable"); click forwards to the control, which the keyboard reaches directly |
| O | 2.5.8 target size | Not applicable | Label is not a control; the associated control keeps its own target (the label's click area is an extra) |
| O | 2.5.3 label in name | Pass | The visible label text is the accessible name (probe below) |
| U | 3.3.2 labels or instructions | Pass | Label text names the control on every story |
| U | 3.2.x predictable | Pass | Click focuses the control and clicks non-text controls only; clicks on links or buttons inside the label are left alone (story `link-inside`, spec) |
| R | 4.1.2 name of the associated control (AX tree, CDP `Accessibility.getFullAXTree`) | Pass | for-input: textbox "Email"; for-checkbox: checkbox "Accept the terms"; wrapping: checkbox "Send me a copy"; with-icon: searchbox "Search" (icon `aria-hidden`, not in the name); disabled: textbox "Account id", disabled; link-inside: checkbox "I agree to the policy" and link "policy" |
| R | Host semantics | Pass | No role on `sb-label`, not exposed as a role, as the contract says |
| R | ID references across shadow roots | Pass (documented limit) | `for` is resolved in the label's own tree scope and `aria-labelledby` is set on the control in that tree. `sb-input` (input in a shadow root) labelled only by `sb-label` gets `aria-labelledby=sb-label-2` on its host but its inner textbox has an empty name in the AX tree; click does focus the inner input. This is the SB-0009 limit stated in contract section 9 and Known drift; the control is named by its own `label` prop |
| R | axe | Pass | Behavior spec: axe clean on default, for-input, for-checkbox, wrapping, with-icon, disabled, link-inside |
| R | Behavior spec and `npm run check` | Pass | 20/20 passed; all checks pass (A1 warn on spec/api.json is unrelated) |
| R | Screen-reader evidence | Pass | AX tree above plus the `__screen-reader__` snapshots (check S1) |

## Failures

None.

### Observation (not a failure, documented)
`sb-label` cannot name a shadow-wrapped `sb-*` control. Contract section 9 point 4 and Known drift already state it, so a consumer is told to use the control's own `label` prop. No change required for stable.

## Verdict
Verdict: ready
Approved-by: Davecelot (2026-11-15)

Names reach the associated controls in the AX tree on every same-tree story, the label is inert for keyboard and AT as a role, forced-colors and contrast hold, axe is clean, the behavior spec (20/20) and `npm run check` pass. The shadow-root limit is by design (SB-0009) and documented.
